  "critique": {
    "axis": "clarity",
    "evidence": "The headline, one-sentence instruction, control/result split, and prominent “Launch Event” CTA make the basic task understandable. The side-by-side ALLOW/BLOCK outcome and risk explanation communicate the intended claim. However, the results appear fully populated before any demonstrated launch state, so users cannot tell whether they are seeing defaults, stale output, or the response to their current controls. Several controls (“TTL delay,” “delegation depth,” “fused risk”) rely on specialist knowledge, and mobile/tablet navigation clips the current Composer location, weakening orientation.",
    "fix": "Give results an explicit state: “Example result” initially, then loading and “Result for this launch” with a timestamp or run ID after submission. Add brief plain-language help for specialist controls and ensure the header visibly identifies Composer at every viewport.",
